  <pre><h1>        Diamond Push-Up / Close-Grip Push-Up</h1></pre>   
  <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u> 
This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates the Diamond Push-Up (Close-Grip Push-Up). The video highlights the triceps, inner chest, and shoulders in bright glowing colors, illustrating how placing your hands close together shifts the mechanical load to maximize triceps and inner chest muscle engagement while maintaining a solid plank position.

Exercise Name: Diamond Push-Up / Close-Grip Push-Up
Target Muscles: Triceps Brachii, Main Chest (Pectoralis Major — Sternal/Inner Head)
Secondary Muscles: Anterior Deltoids (Front Shoulders), Core (Abs & Lower Back)

</div></div>

<h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1><u><b><h4>Step 1: Setup</h4></b></u>
Get into a high plank position with your hands close together directly under your chest. Position your thumbs and index fingers so they touch, forming a diamond or triangle shape.

<u><b><h4>Step 2: Grip & Body Alignment</h4></b></u>
Keep your legs straight, core tight, and your body forming a straight line from head to heels. Do not let your lower back sag.

<u><b><h4>Step 3: Lowering Phase (Eccentric)</h4></b></u>
Inhale as you lower your chest toward your hands in a controlled motion, keeping your elbows tucked close to your torso rather than flaring out.

<u><b><h4>Step 4: Push Phase (Concentric)</h4></b></u>
Exhale as you press firmly through your palms to push your body back up to the starting position, squeezing your triceps and chest at the top lock-out.


<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

<b>◉Triceps Overload:</b> The narrow placement significantly increases elbow flexion demand, making it one of the most effective bodyweight triceps exercises.<br>

<b>◉Inner Chest Squeeze:</b> Narrow hand placement emphasizes the medial/inner fibers of the pectoral muscles during the lock-out phase.<br>

<b>◉No Equipment Needed:</b> High-intensity functional movement that can be performed anywhere using just your body weight.



<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 8 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 6 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep your core engaged throughout the set to prevent hips from sagging or swaying.


